17:["$","p",null,{"children":"An empty log means Bazel never opened a connection, which points at the flag\nrather than at the server."}]
18:["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"other-build-tools","children":"Other build tools"}]
19:["$","p",null,{"children":["The measurement is the same everywhere: build, clean, rebuild, and read the\ntool's own accounting. Only the vocabulary changes. Buck2 shows where each\naction ran in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"buck2 log what-ran"}],"; Pants counts remote cache requests in\nits end-of-run stats when ",["$","code",null,{"children":"[stats].log"}]," is on; recc logs an\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"Action Cache hit"}]," line per compile with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"RECC_LOG_LEVEL=info"}],". Look for\nwhatever your tool calls a cache hit rather than for a Forge-side signal;\nthe server cannot tell you whether the client asked it the right question."]}]
1a:["$","$L2f",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L30",null,{"title":"Zero cache hits, and no errors anywhere","id":"zero-cache-hits-and-no-errors","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["The overwhelmingly common cause is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--remote_instance_name"}],". Forge\nregisters services under the instance names its config lists, and the shipped\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"basic_cas.json5"}]," registers each service twice, once under ",["$","code",null,{"children":"\"\""}]," and once\nunder ",["$","code",null,{"children":"\"main\""}],", precisely so both work. A config that registers only ",["$","code",null,{"children":"main"}],"\nanswers a client that sends the empty instance name with an error,\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"'instance_name' not configured for ''"}],"; Bazel treats a cache error as a\nwarning, prints it once, and builds locally, which reads as zero hits."]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-service/src/ac_server.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-service/src/ac_server.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-service/src/ac_server.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"get_action_result"]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Second most common: the two runs did not use the same digest function. Bazel\nsends SHA-256 by default; if you set ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--digest_function=blake3"}]," on one run and\nnot the other, every digest differs and nothing can hit."]}]]}],["$","$L30",null,{"title":"Hits on the second run, but not from a colleague's machine","id":"hits-locally-but-not-from-another-machine","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Two builds share cache entries only if they produce identical action digests,\nand the digest covers the full command line, the input file contents, ",["$","em",null,{"children":"and"}],"\nthe platform properties. Different compiler versions, different absolute paths\nto the workspace, or a different ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--platforms"}]," value all produce different\ndigests."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["This is the problem remote execution and toolchain pinning exist to solve, and\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/toolchains-and-hermeticity","children":"Toolchains and hermeticity"}],"\ncovers it properly. For a cache-only setup, the practical first step is making\nsure everyone builds with the same toolchain rather than the one on their\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"PATH"}],"."]}]]}],["$","$L30",null,{"title":"The second build is faster but reports no remote hits","id":"faster-but-no-remote-hits","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"bazel clean"}]," removes the output tree but not the repository cache or a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"--disk_cache"}]," if you have one configured, and disk cache hits are counted\nseparately from remote ones. A run that is fast with zero remote hits is\nbeing served locally. Stop Forge and run the build again: if it is\nstill fast, you have been measuring Bazel's local caches the whole time."]}]}],["$","$L30",null,{"title":"Hits disappear after a while","id":"hits-disappear-after-a-while","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Eviction. The shipped example caps the CAS at 10 GB and the action cache at\n1 GB, and a filesystem store evicts least-recently-used content when it\ncrosses the limit. On a real workload those limits are small."}],"$L31"]}]]}]
